    "markdown": "# Project Control Systems\n\n\n\n::: {.callout-note}\nThis chapter is in preparation. The MGMT-3105 course map lists a *Control\nSystems* lecture in this slot; the chapter will be built from project-control\nfundamentals and the course's Project Manager Report and Team Member Report\ntemplates, following the same structure as [Chapter 1](01-Sustainability.qmd)\nand [Chapter 9](09-Cost-Estimation-and-Budgeting.qmd).\n:::\n\n## Learning objectives (planned)\n\nBy the end of this chapter you will be able to:\n\n- Describe the monitoring-and-control loop: measure, compare to baseline, analyse variance, act.\n- Compute earned-value metrics: PV, EV, AC, SV, CV, SPI, CPI.\n- Forecast with EAC, ETC, and TCPI, and interpret the results.\n- Build and read an S-curve of planned vs. earned vs. actual cost.\n- Run integrated change control and keep the baseline meaningful.\n- Report status honestly: the \"watermelon\" trap and leading vs. lagging indicators.\n\n## Topic outline\n\n1. What \"control\" means: closed-loop management.\n2. The performance measurement baseline (scope + schedule + cost).\n3. Earned value management: the three curves and the six core metrics.\n4. Variance analysis and forecasting (EAC scenarios, TCPI).\n5. Change control and configuration management.\n6. Status reporting, dashboards, and honest metrics.\n7. Running case: an earned-value snapshot of the RC-vehicle project at week 8.\n",
